<title>USA: GM names new chief accounting officer.</title>
<headline>GM names new chief accounting officer.</headline>
<dateline>DETROIT 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>General Motors Corp said Thursday it named Peter Bible chief accounting officer and assistant comptroller, effective December 15.</p>
<p>Bible succeeds James Humphrey, who will continue as assistant comptroller, pending a new assignment, GM said.</p>
<p>Bible previously served as assistant comptroller-corporate accounting for GTE Corp.</p>
<p>((--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
